{
 "_doc": [
  "DESTINATION TIERS — exposure, not eligibility (owner's rule, 2026-08-14).",
  "",
  "Every destination in config/seasonality.json leisure_pool can reach a board. What a tier",
  "changes is HOW OFTEN. London, Aruba, Cancun, Paris, New York and Miami should come round",
  "more than San Salvador, without San Salvador disappearing and without the feed showing the",
  "same seven cities every morning.",
  "",
  "Two levers do it, and neither one is a hard filter:",
  "",
  "  repeat_days  How long a destination rests after being posted. A Tier 1 route can come",
  "               back after 2 days, Tier 3 waits 8. That alone makes Tier 1 roughly four",
  "               times as frequent, and it self-balances: on a thin day the rest window is a",
  "               preference, never a filter, so a genuine deal always beats an empty slot.",
  "  bonus        Added to a row's sort score inside a section, so when two fares are close",
  "               the better destination wins the slot. It NEVER touches the price or the",
  "               discount — ordering only. A guaranteed slot can never become an overstated",
  "               saving.",
  "",
  "Reels and Stories take Tier 1 first (see reel_story_tier_floor): those are the highest",
  "reach formats and they should be carrying Aruba, not Wichita.",
  "",
  "Tiers come from CLT-leisure-destinations-ranked.xlsx: 1-25, 26-65, 66+."
 ],
